The available MCP integration is **Pharos MCP** for Pharos chain data and operations; it is not documented as a docs-search server. Add this entry to your MCP client configuration, including Cursor’s MCP configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pharos": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.pharos.xyz/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

It uses Streamable HTTP and requires no API key. If your client only supports `stdio`, use the `mcp-remote` bridge:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pharos": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://mcp.pharos.xyz/mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

See [Pharos MCP](/tooling-and-infrastructure/mcp) for available tools and connection details.

